      "id": 37392,
      "name": "Christopher",
      "username": "Christopher",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/christopher/{size}/1851_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-08-28T13:21:21.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>From <a href=\"http://sentinelsofthemultiverse.com/multiverse/gameplay/glossary\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">The Glossary</a>:</p><p><strong>Environment</strong><span>: An Environment is a deck not played by a player which simulates the environment in which the game takes place. Environments have a deck of 15 Environment cards. Like targets, Environments can be sources of damage, but, unlike targets, the Environments themselves do not have HP and cannot be dealt damage, though some cards in an Environment deck do have HP.</span></p>",
      "post_number": 6,
